  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "term": "Magic ring",
      "definition": "An adjustable loop used as the starting centre of rounds. Pull the tail to close the hole after the first round is joined.",
      "slug": "magic-ring"
    },
    {
      "term": "3-treble cluster (3tr cl)",
      "definition": "Three trebles worked into the same space, each left with the last loop on the hook, then joined together with one yarn-over.",
      "slug": "treble-cluster"
    },
    {
      "term": "V-stitch",
      "definition": "Two trebles into the same space separated by one chain: (tr, ch 1, tr). Creates an open V and increases the stitch count on the side.",
      "slug": "v-stitch"
    },
    {
      "term": "Blocking",
      "definition": "Wetting or steaming finished crochet and pinning to target dimensions while drying. Opens the V-stitch spaces and sharpens corners.",
      "slug": "blocking"
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [
    "magic-ring",
    "working-in-the-round",
    "blocking-crochet"
  ],
  "criticalTechniques": [
    "magic-ring"
  ],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The V-stitch rounds are what separate this eight-round square from a standard extended granny — alternating "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "v-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "V-stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " rows on the sides with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-cluster"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " rows produces a lacy stripe that reads clearly in a single colour. The corner construction stays constant — (3tr cl, ch 2, 3tr cl) — while the side positions alternate between cluster and V-stitch. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " closes the centre. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " opens the V-stitch spaces and makes the stripe pattern sharper."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 75 m per square. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "20 × 20 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook, after blocking. Check at round 4: target 10 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr) — UK: yarn over once"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3-treble cluster (3tr cl)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "V-stitch: (tr, ch 1, tr) into same sp"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first tr throughout. Corners throughout: (3tr cl, ch 2, 3tr cl). V-stitch rounds: replace each side ch-1 sp with (tr, ch 1, tr)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr into ring, ch 2. *(3 tr into ring, ch 2); repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. Pull tail to close ring. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corner sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2 — cluster round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in same corner sp. Ch 1. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 4 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3 — V-stitch round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in same corner sp. Ch 1. *(tr, ch 1, tr) in each side ch-1 sp, ch 1. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. (tr, ch 1, tr) in last side sp. Ch 1. Sl st to top of ch-3. (4 V-stitches on sides, 4 ch-2 corners)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4 — cluster round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in same corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in each ch-1 sp and V-stitch ch-1 sp on side, ch 1 between each group. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Complete side. Sl st to top of ch-3. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 12 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 5 — V-stitch round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As round 3: V-stitch in each side ch-1 sp, cluster corners. Sl st to join. (12 V-stitches on sides, 4 ch-2 corners)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 6 — cluster round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As round 4: cluster in each side sp, cluster corners. Sl st to join. (72 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 20 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 7 — V-stitch round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As round 3: V-stitch in each side ch-1 sp, cluster corners. Sl st to join. (20 V-stitches on sides, 4 ch-2 corners)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 8 — cluster round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As round 4: cluster in each side sp, cluster corners. Sl st to join. Fasten off. (96 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 28 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 8
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Wet-block to 20 × 20 cm, pinning at each corner and along the sides. Blocking opens the V-stitch chain-1 spaces and makes the lacy stripe clearly visible."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join with the slip-stitch method. The V-stitch round on the outer edge (round 7) provides natural joining points — the V-stitch ch-1 spaces align with the ch-1 spaces of adjacent squares when placed right sides together."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 degrees on a gentle cycle. Reshape while damp and dry flat. The V-stitch rounds may close slightly after washing — a light steam-block with a damp cloth will reopen them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Once the alternating round structure is clear, try swapping V-stitches for shells (5 tr into the same ch-1 sp) on the V-stitch rounds for a scalloped stripe effect. Or reverse the pattern — V-stitch corners with cluster sides — for a different geometry."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}